{{ ref: a0d28844-bc75-4c47-ba7b-6eea48b403fc }}
- **Description**: For every non-trivial strongly connected component, suggests the cheapest edge set whose removal makes it acyclic (minimum feedback arc set): exact ILP with lazy cycle constraints (HiGHS) for SCCs ≤ 300 nodes, Eades–Lin–Smyth ordering plus local search above, every suggestion flagged `exact: true|false` (AD-7). When a cyclic group also exceeds the 250-SLOC file cap, the break suggestions become **preconditions of a conditional split**: "break these specific edges first, then this split becomes legal" — the cap is never satisfied by an illegal cyclic split (AD-1).
--{ ref: a0d28844-bc75-4c47-ba7b-6eea48b403fc }--
