{{ ref: 4b1f0f97-61d6-4e48-b703-d8069731cdba }}
```rust
pub struct EdgeBreak {
  pub source: NodeRef,
  pub target: NodeRef,
  pub weight: f64,
  pub exact: bool, // ilp-proven vs heuristic
}

pub struct ConditionalSplit {
  pub scc: Vec<NodeRef>,           // member symbols
  pub preconditions: Vec<EdgeBreak>, // edges to break first
  pub resulting_files: u32,        // split becomes legal after breaking
}
```
--{ ref: 4b1f0f97-61d6-4e48-b703-d8069731cdba }--

{{ ref: 34e27b0e-2bed-4b6c-a62b-24655878800e }}
- **Behaviour**: ILP solves are bounded by `ilp-threshold` (default 300 nodes) and `timeout-seconds` (default 60); on timeout the heuristic answer is returned with `exact: false` — heuristic results never masquerade as proofs. Per-SCC shattering runs rayon-parallel. A single symbol larger than the cap is flagged `oversized symbol` and its file is exempt rather than conditionally splittable.
--{ ref: 34e27b0e-2bed-4b6c-a62b-24655878800e }--
{{ ref: 3fe65ad6-abaf-4bc9-8b4c-87d986a2f875 }}
- **Compatibility**: First release. Tuning `ilp-threshold` or `timeout-seconds` only changes which suggestions are exact, never the legality of any proposed structure.
--{ ref: 3fe65ad6-abaf-4bc9-8b4c-87d986a2f875 }--